<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="005" project="unified-access-control-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-04: Lift the AccessRights.Read ceiling so Write+ policies can pass</title>
    <phase>0 Enforcement Remediation</phase>
    <gate>after-004</gate>
    <status>pending</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies .cs on an authorization path (rights derivation in Spaarke.Dataverse) — FULL per root CLAUDE.md §8.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Rights mapping against a documented ceiling defect with the caller-scoped plumbing already landed by task 004; the fix shape is specified by A-20 evidence.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Rights derivation may require a RetrievePrincipalAccess-style call added to Spaarke.Dataverse/DataverseWebApiService.cs (a known-contended file); conservatively serialized. Even if the fix stays inside DataverseAccessDataSource.cs, this touches the auth-rights spine — merge with /conflict-check.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>001, 004</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, auth, security, dataverse</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Close the Read-ceiling half of finding A-20 (spec FR-04, High): DataverseAccessDataSource.QueryUserPermissionsAsync returns at most AccessRights.Read on success, so EVERY policy requiring more than Read (upload_file = Write|Create, create_container = Create|Write, candownloadfiles, cansharefiles, …) unconditionally denies. Make the snapshot carry the caller's ACTUAL Dataverse rights (Read/Write/Create/Delete/Share/Append) so Write+ policies pass for genuinely authorized users — without over-granting anyone.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in Dataverse Web API access evaluation (RetrievePrincipalAccess semantics) and the Spaarke IAccessDataSource seam. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>An authorized user's access snapshot carries their real rights; canwritefiles / canmanagecontainers succeed for a user with Write/Create in Dataverse; a read-only user is still denied Write+ operations. The rights ceiling defect is gone.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Finding A-20 Read-ceiling half (10-finding-confirmations.md): DataverseAccessDataSource.QueryUserPermissionsAsync:305-379 returns at most a single PermissionRecord(..., AccessRights.Read) on success (:368-372, comment "Grant Read access… Dataverse will enforce Write/Delete separately"); it never returns Write/Create/Delete/Share. upload_file = Write|Create (AuthorizationModule.cs:244-245, OperationAccessPolicy.cs:141) and create_container = Create|Write (:246-247, :147) therefore always deny: (Read &amp; required) != required. Affected endpoints: UploadEndpoints.cs:108,159,214; DocumentsEndpoints.cs:61,106,149,192,245,304,365,418. Task 004 has landed: the data source now receives the caller's token on caller-scoped paths — so real per-principal rights are obtainable (e.g. via RetrievePrincipalAccess or an equivalent caller-scoped rights read). CRITICAL direction: the fix must derive rights from Dataverse's answer FOR THE CALLER; it must not blanket-elevate the app-only path (that would convert a fail-closed defect into an over-grant).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/DataverseAccessDataSource.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/shared/Spaarke.Core/Auth/OperationAccessPolicy.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/AuthorizationModule.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/unit/Spaarke.Core.Tests/Auth/AuthorizationServiceCharacterizationTests.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="001" status="pending">Characterization tests pinning the Read-ceiling denials, flipped here.</dependency>
      <dependency task="004" status="pending">Caller token reaches the data source — real per-principal rights are queryable.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-003">Fail closed: an error resolving rights yields NO rights (deny), never a default grant. On the app-only path, rights above Read MUST NOT be granted by inference from app visibility. Scope: QueryUserPermissionsAsync and every path it feeds.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Rights are derived from the caller-scoped Dataverse answer (OBO), consistent with the task-004 model. Scope: the rights-derivation mechanism chosen here.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The snapshot must never EXCEED the caller's actual Dataverse rights on the record. Scope: all mapping code added by this task.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Spaarke.Dataverse is consumed by the BFF (CLAUDE.md §10): report publish size vs ~44.96 MB baseline in PR; ceiling 60 MB (NFR-06). Scope: this task's PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="task-003">BINDING: task 003 registered "entity.associate_document" requiring AccessRights.AppendTo -- the FIRST use of that flag in OperationAccessPolicy. When lifting the Read ceiling in DataverseAccessDataSource.QueryUserPermissionsAsync:305-379 you MUST map Dataverse AppendToAccess -> AccessRights.AppendTo (and AppendAccess -> AccessRights.Append). Mapping only Read/Write/Delete/Create/Share leaves POST /api/office/save permanently 403 while LOOKING fixed: the operation resolves, so the denial reads as a legitimate insufficient_rights rather than the loud unknown_operation it replaced -- a silent failure that is worse than the bug it succeeded. Add a test asserting a caller with AppendTo on the target entity is ALLOWED entity.associate_document. Rationale: notes/task-003-operation-rights-decisions.md section 2. Scope: the rights-mapping change.</constraint>
    <constraint source="task-006">Task 006 made GET /api/documents/{id}/permissions caller-scoped, and its capability booleans are projected from the SAME snapshot this task widens. Until the ceiling lifts, ELEVEN of the fourteen capabilities (CanDownload, CanUpload, CanReplace, CanDelete, CanUpdateMetadata, CanShare, CanRestoreVersion, CanMove, CanCopy, CanCheckOut, CanCheckIn) are false for every caller in production -- only CanPreview, CanReadMetadata and CanViewVersions can be true. When this task lands, verify those flags actually light up for a caller holding the corresponding rights; a Read-ceiling fix that does not surface in the capabilities response means the snapshot widened somewhere the endpoint does not read. Mapping table: notes/task-006-capability-rights-mapping.md section 2. Scope: verification of this task's rights-mapping change.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Dataverse principal rights mapping</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-003-authorization-seams.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/auth.md</file>
      <file>projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/investigation/10-finding-confirmations.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="dataverse-obo" location=".claude/patterns/auth/dataverse-obo.md">OBO access to Dataverse Web API</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load knowledge files; declare FULL rigor. Confirm task 004 is merged.</step>
    <step order="1">Read QueryUserPermissionsAsync:305-379 and GetUserAccessAsync:159-227; identify where the Read cap is applied in both SP and OBO modes.</step>
    <step order="2">Implement caller-scoped rights derivation: query Dataverse for the caller's actual AccessRights on the record (RetrievePrincipalAccess or equivalent) and map the full flag set into the snapshot. Preserve the OBO/SP mode split from task 004.</step>
    <step order="3">Verify the app-only mode does NOT gain rights above what it had — app visibility must not imply Write.</step>
    <step order="4">Flip characterization tests; add positive tests (Write-holder passes upload_file / create_container policy evaluation) and negative tests (Read-only holder denied).</step>
    <step order="5">Run full test suite; build green.</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="7">Document the rights-mapping table (Dataverse right → AccessRights flag) in projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If deriving real rights adds Dataverse round trips beyond the existing per-request budget (NFR-02 spirit), STOP and escalate with measurements before adding a per-operation query.</trigger>
    <trigger>If any existing consumer DEPENDS on the Read ceiling (i.e., would newly grant Write somewhere unaudited), STOP and list those consumers for review before merging.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools><tool name="dotnet">Build + test</tool></tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/DataverseAccessDataSource.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Spaarke.Core.Tests/Auth/AuthorizationServiceCharacterizationTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A caller holding Write/Create on the record passes canwritefiles (upload_file = Write|Create) and canmanagecontainers (create_container = Create|Write) policy evaluation (FR-04 acceptance).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a caller holding only Read is denied upload_file and create_container.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a caller with NO access to the record receives an empty/deny snapshot (no rights).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: an error during rights resolution denies — no default rights are granted.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The snapshot never exceeds the caller's actual Dataverse rights (asserted by test with a mocked Dataverse answer).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All unit tests pass; build green; publish size reported in PR and ≤60 MB.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-04; finding A-20 Read-ceiling half (policy keys are task 003). File-disjoint from task 006 (PermissionsEndpoints) but conservatively parallel-safe:false because the rights read may extend DataverseWebApiService.cs.</notes>

  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill></execution>
</task>
